# THE WORK EDITOR, which is the generic editor pointed at work.
#
# The format is Obsidian's and the engine renders it. Nothing here is a second
# grammar, and nothing in the renderer knows what a token is.
#
# A DECLARED GROUP IS ALWAYS DRAWN, with nothing in it if nothing matches. What
# it names goes on existing whether or not a token is in that state today, and a
# heading that comes and goes is a heading nobody can aim at. A group nobody
# declared comes from the data, and one of those is gone the moment it empties.
#
# THE STATES ARE THE PROCESS'S AND THIS FILE NAMES THEM BY HAND. The engine held
# eleven states and this file listed all eleven; now a process file declares its
# own, and a .base file cannot ask the engine for a set. So a process that
# invents a state needs a group here, and until then its tokens draw under the
# group the data makes, which is a heading that disappears when it empties.
#
# TWO KINDS OF GROUP, AND THE PAGE DRAWS BOTH.
#
# A QUERY IS A FILTER AND NOT A PLACE. It is declared below, it is always drawn
# whether or not anything matches, and a row draws under every query that takes
# it. That is what the states and the processes are.
#
# A BUCKET IS WHERE A PERSON PUT A ROW. The grouping is by the bucket, so a
# person can drag a handful of tokens under a heading of their own and none of
# them moves. It groups by nothing else: it read if(bucket, bucket, status)
# once, so a token with no bucket grouped under its state and drew a second
# group beside the query named after that state.
#
# A COLUMN IS NAMED WHAT THE NOTE NAMES IT. displayName exists for a heading
# the owner wants to read differently, and renaming status to state or holder to
# who is not that: it hides where the value came from and nobody can filter on a
# word that is not in the file.
properties:
  title:
    opensNote: true

# EVERY NOTE THIS SCHEMA READS, AND NONE THAT HAS ENDED. A disposition is the
# ending, so one test answers it whatever the process calls its last state.
filters:
  and:
    - kind == "work-token"
    - disposition == ""

groups:
  # YOURS IS WHAT WAITS FOR A PERSON. There is no assignee: which agent does the
  # work was never something anybody read, and the one thing a queue has to know
  # is whether a person has to look at it.
  - name: yours
    filter: needs_human == "true"

  # AND ONE GROUP PER STATE THE note PROCESS DECLARES, from
  # src/processes/note.process.yaml.
  #
  # THERE IS NO GROUP PER PROCESS. With one process and one open state, a query
  # on the process and a query on the state answer the same set, and two
  # headings over one set of rows is two things a reader has to tell apart for
  # no reason. Add one when a second process makes the two answers differ.
  #
  # AND THERE IS NO here. It asked who holds a token, which was worth a heading
  # while a hold was a standing thing an agent took up and kept. A hold lasts
  # from one call to the next now, because se apply and se run name their token
  # on the write, so the group was empty whenever nobody was mid-command.
  - name: noted
    filter: status == "noted"

pinned:
  - yours

views:
  - type: table
    name: left
    counts:
      - name: in hand
        filter: holder != ""
        outOf: disposition == ""
      - name: waiting for a person
        filter: needs_human == "true"
        outOf: disposition == ""
    order:
      - title
      - status
      - process
      - holder
    columnSize:
      title: 300
      status: 110
      process: 90
      bucket: 90
      holder: 71
      blocked: 543
    # THE GROUPING IS BY BUCKET, and a drop writes one. The queries above are
    # the other kind of group and they need no level: a declared group is a
    # filter, and the grouping is what a person arranges by hand.
    groupBy:
      - property: bucket
        sets: bucket
        direction: ASC
    collapsed:
      - noted
    sort:
      - property: title
        direction: DESC
  - type: table
    name: right
    counts:
      - name: in hand
        filter: holder != ""
        outOf: disposition == ""
    order:
      - title
      - status
    groupBy:
      - property: bucket
        sets: bucket
        direction: ASC
    collapsed:
      - noted
